 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Talk and write",
   "texto": [
    "The **Perfekt**: **Ich habe gestern gearbeitet** (yesterday I worked) is used in the daily conversation. In written texts, stories and news, the **Präteritum**: **Gestern arbeitete ich lange** is used (I worked a lot yesterday).",
    "With **sein**, **haben** and manners, the Präteritum is also used in the conversation: **Ich hatte keine Zeit** (I didn't have time)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "When, in the past",
   "texto": [
    "**Als** means «when» in the past and is used once: **Als ich klein war, wohnte ich in Madrid** (when I was a kid I lived in Madrid). The verb of the sentence with «als» goes to the end.",
    "Do not confuse with **wenn** (when, if, present or future)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Sort the story",
   "texto": [
    "**Zuerst** (first), **dann** (then), **danach** (after that) and **schließlich** (at last) mark the order of the facts.",
    "Example: **Zuerst ging ich in die Schule, dann kam ich nach Hause.**"
   ]
  },
